akantu-rs oracle VARIANT patch ud031 — anisotropic damage: zero-initialise A_diag

NOT applied to the regular oracle builds (oracle/patches/variants/ is outside
the oracle/patches/*.patch glob of oracle/scripts/in-container/build.sh).
Upstream: akantu 35a851780d0b9471d258ed53a003ae98aaa95ea0
Defect: UD-031 (docs/UPSTREAM_DEFECTS.md, category A for this part: undefined
behaviour is compared against a patched oracle, D-003). In the anonymous
helper tensorPlusOp of material_anisotropic_damage_tmpl.hh the diagonal
matrix `Matrix<Real, dim, dim> A_diag;` is not initialised and only its
diagonal is written before `A_directions * A_diag * A_directions.transpose()`,
so every tensorPlus / tensorSqrt result (the damage increment, sqrt(1 - D))
reads stack contents through the off-diagonal entries. The material-wide
E / nu rewrite of the broken (tension) branch then propagates it to the
elastic tangent (review V64 MX2-08, blocker B-015: three identical x86_64
runs gave two tangents). The patch only adds the missing zero-initialisation
(one line, no other change), so a build with it is the defined-behaviour
reference of the akantu-rs port (which zero-initialises unconditionally) for
the cases fixtures/material/anisotropic_damage_mazars/variant_ud031/*.
This patch alone does NOT remove every uninitialised read of the law
(correction after review V100 MX3-01): once UD-763 has made D NaN, the 3-D
`tensorSqrt(1 - D)` hands a NaN 3 x 3 matrix to Eigen's EigenSolver, which
returns NoConvergence without writing its eigenpairs, and Akantu's
MatrixBase::eig ignores the status and returns them uninitialised (UD-814;
valgrind: 686 reads in variant_ud031/3d_uniaxial on a build with this patch
only). That read is masked in every recorded quantity (it only enters
sqrt(1 - D), which multiplies the never-written elastic stress; the stress is
NaN through (1 - D):sigma_el whatever the eigenpairs are, unless they hold a
NaN with a payload) and is defined by the companion patch
ud814-eig-noconvergence-zero-init.patch, which the variant build applies
after this one. Apart from that: Dtmp is written before every use,
TrD_n_1_tmp, the threshold and equivalent-strain parameters have in-class
initialisers, and the eigen outputs are written whenever the solver
converges (1-D/2-D solves of a NaN matrix end with NumericalIssue after
writing every eigenvalue and the Schur vectors).
How to build the variant on boat: oracle/scripts/build-ud031-variant.sh
(patches the sandbox copy of /build/src-strict with both patches, rebuilds
the strict library and installs it with its install RUNPATH; the probe
environment then records the patched files in each manifest's
reference.patches). Documented in docs/ORACLE_BUILD.md section 12.1.

--- a/src/model/solid_mechanics/materials/material_damage/material_anisotropic_damage_tmpl.hh
+++ b/src/model/solid_mechanics/materials/material_damage/material_anisotropic_damage_tmpl.hh
@@ -98,6 +98,7 @@
                     Eigen::MatrixBase<D2> & A_directions, Op && oper) {
     Vector<Real, dim> A_eigs;
     Matrix<Real, dim, dim> A_diag;
+    A_diag.zero(); // akantu-rs UD-031 variant: zero-initialise
     A.eig(A_eigs, A_directions);
 
     for (auto && [i, eig] : enumerate(A_eigs)) {
